.TH DR-CHARM 1 "2026-09-04" "dr-charm" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dr-charm \- DragonRealms terminal client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dr-charm
.RB [ -c | --config " " \fIPATH\fR ]
.br
.B dr-charm
.RB [ -V | --version ]
.br
.B dr-charm
.RB [ -h | --help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dr-charm
signs in to DragonRealms with an existing account and character, then renders a
terminal interface with an inline dashboard.
Game, system, command, agent, whisper, and familiar output stays in the
terminal's native scrollback. Familiar messages use a \fB[familiar]\fR label.
The dashboard shows the current location and exits, left and right hands, a
prepared spell when present, and connection and logging state. Connection state
remains visible while the session closes or reconnects.
.SH INTERFACE
.TP
.B Enter
Send the command line.
.TP
.B Up, Down
Recall commands from the current session.
.TP
.B Ctrl-G
Open the current input in \fB$VISUAL\fR or \fB$EDITOR\fR.
.TP
.B Escape
Enter map navigation when the learned map is visible. Leave help or the theme
selector. In map navigation, return to command entry.
.TP
.B Tab
Return from map navigation to command entry.
.TP
.B h, l, j, k, Ctrl-U, Ctrl-D, g, G
Pan a visible learned map horizontally, vertically, by half a screen, or to its
top or bottom while map navigation is active.
.TP
.B F1
Show help.
.TP
.B F3
Select a theme.
.TP
.B F4
Toggle session logging.
.TP
.B F6
Toggle auto mode. Enabling it does not make a model request. While auto mode is
on and the status bar shows \fBREADY\fR, Enter whispers to the agent instead of
sending a game command.
.TP
.B Ctrl-C
Quit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " PATH"
Read credentials from PATH instead of the XDG default configuration file.
.TP
.BI -c " PATH"
Short form of \fB--config\fR.
.TP
.B --version
Print the installed version without reading configuration or opening a network
connection.
.TP
.B -V
Short form of \fB--version\fR.
.TP
.B --help
Print help to standard output.
.TP
.B -h
Short form of \fB--help\fR.
.SH ALIASES
\fBdr-charm\fR expands the first word of a command when it matches a built-in
alias. It sends other commands unchanged.
.TP
.B n, s, e, w, ne, nw, se, sw, u, d, o
Movement aliases for north, south, east, west, diagonals, up, down, and out.
.TP
.B l, i, sta, kne, sit, ly, hi, sn, sea
Aliases for look, inventory, stand, kneel, sit, lie, hide, sneak, and search.
.TP
.B att, ki, sk, arr, loot
Aliases for attack, kill, skin, arrange, and \fBloot all\fR.
.SH AUTO MODE
Auto mode is available when the configuration file contains an \fBagent\fR block.
It starts off. Press F6 to enable it. Once the status bar shows \fBREADY\fR, a
new DragonRealms prompt or a whisper wakes the agent. The agent may reply in
the client, choose one game command, or wait for a game event or player whisper.
.PP
Whispers and replies use bold text with reverse-video \fB[whisper]\fR and
\fB[agent]\fR labels. Agent commands start with \fB[agent] >\fR.
.PP
The block accepts \fBendpoint\fR, \fBapi_key\fR, \fBmodel\fR, and
\fBcharacter\fR. The endpoint is the complete HTTP or HTTPS URL and its path
must end in \fB/responses\fR. The API key is optional. The other three values
are required when the block is present. The URL cannot contain embedded
credentials or a fragment.
.PP
The endpoint must support streaming OpenAI Responses requests and function
tools. Chat Completions endpoints are not supported. \fBdr-charm\fR does not
set a reasoning effort or service tier.
.PP
Every request sends recent game and familiar text from terminal scrollback to
the configured endpoint.
Requests may also include the configured agent character, earlier agent
conversation, and whispers. Use an endpoint you trust. When that conversation
grows long, \fBdr-charm\fR asks the endpoint to summarize its older parts. It
does not add your DragonRealms account or password to requests.
.PP
The status bar shows \fBAGENT off\fR, \fBAGENT idle\fR,
\fBAGENT thinking\fR, \fBAGENT waiting\fR, \fBAGENT paused\fR, or
\fBAGENT error\fR. A waiting agent wakes for a prompt or whisper. A paused
agent wakes only for a whisper. F6 cancels a request when turning auto mode
off. Turning it on again restores prompt-driven behavior. A new eligible wake
cancels the current request before starting another one. Disconnecting or
quitting also cancels it. The client discards agent conversation when it exits.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dr-charm/config.yaml
Default configuration file containing account credentials and optional agent
settings. A first run without configuration writes a commented template with
owner-only permissions, then exits.
When \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR is unset, use \fI~/.config/dr-charm/config.yaml\fR.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dr-charm/themes
Custom theme JSON files. When \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR is unset, use
\fI~/.config/dr-charm/themes\fR.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/dr-charm/logs
Session transcripts. When \fBXDG_STATE_HOME\fR is unset, use
\fI~/.local/state/dr-charm/logs\fR. New directories are owner-only and
\fBdr-charm\fR retains up to 30 closed logs and 100 MiB as soft limits.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/dr-charm/maps/Map00_Learned.xml
Learned Genie-compatible map XML. When \fBXDG_DATA_HOME\fR is unset, use
\fI~/.local/share/dr-charm/maps/Map00_Learned.xml\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VISUAL
Command used by Ctrl-G. Takes precedence over \fBEDITOR\fR.
.TP
.B EDITOR
Command used by Ctrl-G when \fBVISUAL\fR is unset.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Absolute base directory for the credential file and custom themes.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Absolute base directory for session transcripts.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Absolute base directory for the learned map.
.SH SECURITY
Configuration files contain account credentials. Session logs contain
character and gameplay data. New configuration files and logs are readable
only by their owner. \fBdr-charm\fR leaves permissions on existing
configuration files unchanged.
